From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 23:47:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] initcpio: Add the dwc3-apple glue module

Since the dwc3-apple glue driver went upstream, the Apple Type-C DWC3
controllers bind to it instead of dwc3-of-simple. Nothing pulls it in
on its own: it depends on dwc3 and phy-apple-atc, and no module
depends on it. The hook adds dwc3 but not the glue, so in the
initramfs the controllers stay unbound and register no USB role
switch. The Type-C port controllers (tps6598x, sn201202x) then defer
until the root filesystem's udev loads dwc3-apple, and a USB keyboard
on a USB-C port cannot type an encrypted root's passphrase.

Add dwc3-apple next to dwc3.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 initcpio/install/asahi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/initcpio/install/asahi b/initcpio/install/asahi
index 31730ac..3e2b619 100644
--- a/initcpio/install/asahi
+++ b/initcpio/install/asahi
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@ build() {
     map add_module macsmc? macsmc-rtkit?
 
     # For USB
-    map add_module i2c-pasemi-platform? tps6598x? sn201202x? apple-dart? dwc3? dwc3-of-simple? \
+    map add_module i2c-pasemi-platform? tps6598x? sn201202x? apple-dart? dwc3? dwc3-apple? dwc3-of-simple? \
         nvmem-apple-efuses? phy-apple-atc? xhci-plat-hcd? xhci-pci? pcie-apple? gpio_macsmc?
 
     # For HID
-- 
